{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>After HaShem your Elohim you shall walk.</b> After His attributes, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 28): ״והלכת בדרכיו״ — <b>and Him you shall fear,</b> from investigating His essence from the side of His very essence, but only from the side of His actions." "<b>And His commandments you shall keep.</b> This is the Written Torah, which is תרי״ג (613) commandments." "<b>And His voice you shall hear.</b> These are the prophets. And this too includes the Oral Torah, which is a tradition (kabbalah) from the prophets, in the manner of what we learned: Mosheh received Torah from Sinai and handed it on to Yehoshua, and Yehoshua to the elders, and the elders to the prophets, and the prophets handed it on to the men of the Great Assembly." "<b>And Him you shall serve,</b> this is prayer. <b>And in Him you shall cleave.</b> That even at the time you are occupied with permissible matters, you shall bind your thought to Him and not separate from Him even for a single hour." "<b>Or</b> one may say, ״ובו תדבקון״ — that you should not wish to depart from His service ever. For in the way of the world, when a servant is under the hand of his master — even if the master were good and compassionate toward him — he still longs to separate from him, to go out from his authority a free man for himself. Therefore it says here ״ובו תדבקון״ — that you shall cleave to His service and not crave separation and freedom from Him, for His service is the true freedom." "<b>Or</b> it is possible to say further: ״ובו תדבקון״ — and to Him you shall cleave — is the promise of the reward of the World to Come. And it comes to teach that if we fulfill the admonitions he has mentioned — namely, that we follow His attributes, that we fear Him, that we keep the Written Torah and the Oral Torah, and that we serve Him in prayer — He promises us that we shall be cleaving to Him in the end. And cleaving to Him is that one cleaves to the holy El, which is the reward of the World to Come."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:05.503966985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}